Return `false` from the `_.transform` callback to stop iteration early. The callback receives `(accumulator, value, key, object)` and can mutate the accumulator before returning:

```javascript
const result = _.transform([2, 3, 4], (acc, n) => {
  acc.push(n * n);

  if (n === 3) {
    return false; // stop iterating
  }
}, []);

console.log(result); // [4, 9]
```

Returning other values continues iteration.
